  "worked_solution": "An implication $A\u21d2B$ is true *unless* $A$ is true and $B$ is false. In other words, the implication is true unless the \"promise\" is broken.\n\n- Statement I is true. The antecedent $-5>-2$ is false, so the promise does not apply. Regardless of the consequent, the promise is *not* broken, and the statement is true.\n\n- Statement II is true. The antecedent $-5<-2$ is true, and the consequent $-2<-1$ is true. So the promise is kept, and the statement is true.\n\n- Statement III is true. Again, the antecedent $-5>-2$ is false, so the promise does not apply. Regardless of the consequent, the promise is *not* broken, and the statement is true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\"",
